  "chapter": 801,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 152 Chapter 801\n \n         MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 155, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the state administrative procedure act, in relation\n        to  public  hearings  on  proposed  rules; and providing for the\n        repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill will allow agencies to utilize innovative techniques whenev-\ner they are required to hold a hearing on any rule or regulation.  These\ntechniques  include  allowing  the  public  to  ask  questions of agency\npersonnel for a portion of such hearing, organizing such  hearing  as  a\nroundtable  discussion,  scheduling  an  evening or weekend hearing, and\nusing broadcasting and teleconferencing technologies.  These  techniques\nwill  serve  to  advance the very worthy goal of expanding opportunities\nfor public participation in public meetings.\n \n  This bill was first introduced in the legislature almost thirty  years\nago  and  there  are  portions of this bill that were problematic from a\nprogrammatic and operational standpoint for  the  agencies.  However,  I\nhave  worked  with  the  legislature  and  they have agreed to introduce\nlegislation in the upcoming session  that  will  address  and  alleviate\nthese concerns.  Based upon this understanding, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
